    *   Since the row lengths are heavily imbalanced, a simple `#pragma omp parallel for` might lead to poor load balancing.
    *   The total work is proportional to the number of non-zero elements (`nnz`).
    *   The work for each row $i$ is `rowptr[i+1] - rowptr[i]`.

    *   *Static Scheduling:* `schedule(static)` divides the rows equally. This will be slow because a few threads will get the "heavy" rows and others will finish quickly.
